    "opening": "Studio Ajid is an <strong>interior design studio</strong> in Doha where <strong>art and craftsmanship</strong> sit at the centre of the work. We draw on familiar elements of <strong>Qatari homes</strong> and reinterpret them in a contemporary language that reflects our own identity.",
    "intro": {
      "note": "Established 2026 — Doha, Qatar",
      "body": "The studio is designed entirely without doors, so the spaces stay visually connected and the interior feels open. Privacy comes instead from the placement of walls and the orientation of each opening. The palette is drawn from Qatar's landscape — the deep blue of the sea, and the tones of sand, earth and limestone."
    },
    "chapter1": {
      "heading": "Familiar forms,\nmade new",
      "body": "The terrazzo flooring recalls the light, speckled courtyard tiles found in older Qatari homes. The entrance partition takes its rhythm from traditional mashrabiya screens, carrying a custom pattern derived from the studio's own visual identity.",
      "note": "→ Est. 2026\nDoha, Qatar",
      "noteLink": "[Studio]"
    },
    "chapter2": {
      "heading": "Art at the centre of the space",
      "note": "Terrazzo • Mashrabiya • Porcelain • Limestone",
      "quote": "Art is not placed in the space afterwards — it is part of how the space was conceived.",
      "quoteSource": "[Studio Ajid — Design Concept]",
      "body": "The interior holds a collection of porcelain pieces designed by Studio Ajid with a French porcelain house in Limoges — work that carries the studio's regard for local identity and fine craftsmanship.",
      "caption": "Porcelain collection • Limoges"
    },
    "chapter3": {
      "body": "The window openings reference traditional forms, while their black finish sets them in bold contrast against the pale surfaces around them.",
      "note1": "All original artworks are by Qatari artist Essa, founder of ESSA Art Studio and a partner in Studio Ajid.",
      "note2": "Terrazzo • Mashrabiya • Porcelain • Sea, sand and limestone"
    },
    "closing": {
      "caption": "Studio Ajid • Doha"
    },
    "closingStatement": "Familiar forms, read again in a contemporary hand — so a space belongs to where it stands."
  },
